\subtree{
\title{10. The prototype: what was measured}

\p{Private tree \code{\verb~|work/u2/tree/rlvm-machine~} = the main tree of 19:04:34Z + the patches of \code{\verb~|work/u2/patches/~} (eight main files, 667 added and 9 removed lines, one test class). One binary for before and after: the mode is the system property \code{\verb~|rlvm.u2~}; the pristine twin (\code{\verb~|work/u2/base~}) is measured beside it to show that the mode-off prototype is the tree it was copied from. Switches everywhere: the default set of that tree (\code{\verb~|gated, pchk, expect, warm, code, casetrees, bodies, directrules, same, match, joint, lazycases, lazyeval~}).}

\subtree{
\title{10.1 Counts (JVM launcher, ONE worker, statistics file; \code{\verb~|work/u2/counts/~}, table by \code{\verb~|work/u2/scripts/tab.py~})}

\p{One run per row (jar \code{\verb~|16542003a4cc~}; rows 107 and 111: the jar with adaptive sites, \code{\verb~|879b493003e3~}, which is the same code with bit 64 off). Deltas are against the mode-off row of the corpus. "never identified" = private applications that were in no table when their session ended: each is a probe of \code{\verb~|vtab~} (hash, table load, comparison or insert) and a table entry that the mode-off machine paid for and nothing ever used.}

\table{
