}

\p{This sizes stage D (lazy suspensions): a suspension that is forced, tabled or inferred needs its identity (its memo is the point of it), so the population a lazy suspension could spare is the second column: 2-6 \% of the suspensions on library corpora and 0.18 M records on reachability (two probes each, against 3.0 M application probes). \strong{Lazy closures and suspensions are not worth their mechanism (private frames) today.}}
}

