}

\p{Reading (a difference is called resolved only where the two ranges do not overlap; with two processes per row that is thin, and the scatter between two processes of one configuration is up to 8 \% on the JVM - J1 and J2 put the pristine jar 4 \% below and 9 \% above the mode-off prototype):}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Reachability, JVM.} One worker: block sites lazy (43) -13 \% in two windows (J1 mode 11: 902 against 1036 ms, ranges disjoint; JA: 930 against 1066); in large sessions only (171) -16.5 \%; with adaptive sites (235) \strong{-16.7 \% (888 against 1066 ms, ranges disjoint)}; every site (47, J1) -23 \%, every site adaptive (111, JA) -16.5 \%. Eight workers: 43: -8.1 \% (480 against 522 ms; the workers' CPU -12.4 \%); \strong{235: -10.0 \% (460 against 511 ms; CPU -10.5 \%)}; the ranges touch (439-505 against 492-553). With eight workers the wall clock of this corpus is its largest declaration, so the workers' CPU is the better witness of the mechanism.}
\li{\strong{Cedar slice, JVM.} Block sites lazy in every session (43): +4.0 \% and +4.3 \% at one worker in two windows (ranges overlapping both times), +1.9 \% at eight; every site lazy (47): \strong{+9.1 \% at one worker (resolved)}, +6.0 \% at eight. In large sessions only (171): -0.1 \% at one worker, -5.8 \% at eight (inside the scatter: 188-212 against 195-255) - and its counters ARE the mode-off counters (10.1), so "no change" is by construction.}
\li{\strong{Where the gain comes from, and where the loss.} The same mechanism on two corpora: reachability's records are made in a few sessions of hundreds of thousands to millions of records (85 \% of its lazy constructions happen in sessions of 2^17 records and more; intern tables of several to tens of MiB; NOTES-M1 5.3: four fifths of a probe is the cache miss of the table slot), the Cedar slice's in sessions that are reset at 1 MiB (tables in the cache). A probe that is not made is worth a cache miss in the first and almost nothing in the second, where the bit tests of the key-forming loops and the duplicate records are what remains. Hence bit 128.}
\li{\strong{Reachability, native image} (NB). One worker: 43: -5.5 \% (1271 against 1345 ms, ranges overlapping), 171: -8.2 \%, \strong{235: -11.9 \% (1185 against 1345 ms; 1161-1245 against 1273-1419: disjoint)}. \strong{Eight workers: no gain} - 43: +6.5 \%, 171: +3.6 \%, 235: +3.1 \%, 239: -0.9 \%, every one inside the scatter of the mode-off rows (587-652 ms); the workers' CPU is -0.4 to -4.9 \%. On the JVM the same modes are -8 to -10 \% at eight workers with the workers' CPU -10 to -12 \%. So the owner's first number - warm wall clock with eight workers - moves on the JVM (at the edge of the scatter of two processes) and does not move in the image; the gain that is resolved on both platforms is the one-worker gain. Why eight workers of the image lose what one worker gains is not known (candidates, not measured: the record and run slabs grow by a third and are grown by copying, which costs the serial collector of the image more when eight threads allocate; memory bandwidth shared by eight workers writing a third more).}
\li{\strong{Cedar slice, native image, eight workers}: 43: +5.8 \% (workers' CPU +6.4 \%), 171: +0.4 \%: as on the JVM.}
\li{\strong{Not resolved by these windows}: the difference between 43 and 171 / 235 on reachability (171 should be 43 minus the lazy constructions of small sessions; it measures 4 points better at one worker and 5 worse at eight: scatter); why every-site laziness is that much better at one worker on reachability (J1) although it identifies more records than block-site laziness.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{10.3 Gates}

\p{All on the private tree, reports under the private root \code{\verb~|work/u2/root~\verb~|/work/status/~} (never the project's \code{\verb~|work/status/~}), M8's harness started by \code{\verb~|work/u2/scripts/m8.sh~} (\code{\verb~|rlvm.machine.M8Main gate -~} with \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.u2=N~}, so that EVERY machine of the gate's JVM - all six lanes, the generic tier lane and the driver of part 5 - runs the mode), switch set = the tree's default.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Gate}\th{Mode}\th{Result}}
\tr{\td{M8's full gate (\code{\verb~|machine-gate-default-u47-u47.md~}, 750 s, final classes)}\td{\strong{47} (every site lazy, K + M + C)}\td{\strong{PASS WITH DECLINES.} (1) differential per declaration against the reference engine: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0 on tutorial (395 units), bugs (1,428), all 230 tests (17,493 units; 15,800 accepted, 40 rejected, 5 declined), Init (57,774 accepted, 164 declined), Std (99,893 / 203), reachability (4,216 / 8), the Cedar slice (8,053 / 11); (2) tier equivalence with the generic tier: 0 declarations with another outcome, 0 with another reason; \code{\verb~|M8Tiers~} values 700 + 5,944 results, 0 different; (3) convention equivalence, host depth 0 and unbounded against 128 (outcome, reason, ticks, call events, trace, every record word, run word and pair): 0 different; (4) audit lanes \code{\verb~|poison,scopeaudit,maskaudit~} and \code{\verb~|memocheck,shortcheck~}: 0 different outcomes, 0 E_AUDIT; (5) the real driver: 230 / 230 verdicts right, the four corpora accepted with 4 workers, MACHINE-INCOMPLETE 0, WARM-ANOMALY 0, disagreements 0. Every decline is the tree's own eager-reduction decline (S-F5's rule)}}
\tr{\td{the same gate (\code{\verb~|machine-gate-default-u11-u11.md~}, 856 s; classes of 19:36Z: scrutinee rule, class M = WHNF only)}\td{\strong{11} (block sites, K + M)}\td{\strong{PASS WITH DECLINES}, the same zeros in all five parts, the same declines}}
\tr{\td{the same gate, final classes}\td{\strong{43} (block sites, K + M + C: the form recommended for stage 1)}\td{\strong{PASS WITH DECLINES} (\code{\verb~|machine-gate-default-u43-u43.md~}, 915 s): differential SOUNDNESS 0 / COMPLETENESS 0 on every corpus (the accepted / rejected / declined counts of the mode-47 row), tier equivalence 0 / 0 and 0 different values, convention equivalence 0 different, audits 0 / 0, pipeline 230 / 230 right, MACHINE-INCOMPLETE 0, WARM-ANOMALY 0}}
\tr{\td{M8's full gate (\code{\verb~|machine-gate-default-u235-u235.md~}, 586 s; the classes the timings were taken with)}\td{\strong{235} (block sites, K + M + C, adaptive sites, large sessions only: stage 1)}\td{\strong{PASS WITH DECLINES}, the same zeros in all five parts; the ticks of reachability (9,104,125), Init and Std in its differential part are the mode-off ticks}}
\tr{\td{the same gate on the tree of the patches (force points outlined; \code{\verb~|machine-gate-default-u235r-u235r.md~})}\td{\strong{235}}\td{\strong{PASS WITH DECLINES} (698 s): the same zeros in all five parts, and the tick totals of its differential part are those of the row above in every corpus (tutorial 4,705, bugs 86,551, all 230 tests 264,223,400, Init 39,328,357, Std 64,280,298, reachability 9,104,125, Cedar slice 9,987,067): the outlining changed nothing that is counted}}
\tr{\td{the hostile suite of the soundness review: \code{\verb~|SHostileSlowTest~} (32 switch sets x 329 exports = 10,528 judgments, each against the official verdict of the manifest; the strict \code{\verb~|noKnownFindingIsLeft~}) and \code{\verb~|SHostileTest~}, test JVM with \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.u2=47~} (\code{\verb~|work/u2/logs/hostile-u47.out~})}\td{\strong{47}}\td{\strong{0 unexpected verdicts, 0 known findings open, 0 declines of the machine} under every switch set}}
\tr{\td{the hostile suite on the tree of the patches, \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.u2=235 -Drlvm.u2.big=8~} (threshold 2^8 records, so that the mode engages in exports of a few hundred records; \code{\verb~|work/u2/logs/hostileR-u235.out~})}\td{\strong{235}}\td{32 switch sets x 329 exports: \strong{0 unexpected verdicts, 0 declines}; \code{\verb~|SHostileTest~} 6 / 6}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|U2ValuesTest~} (own hostile cases, 6 tests; patch 0007 as \code{\verb~|M1LazyIdTest~})}\td{3, 15, 47, 3 + 64}\td{green: (a) 6,000 random constructions per seed - lazy, interned, extended, captured into frames, across table growth, with and without adaptive sites: after identification one canonical id per structure and one structure per canonical id, no private component in any key, \code{\verb~|vtabUsed~} = table entries = records that are not private, clean tables after the reset; (b) flags of private applications = flags of interned ones; (c) nests 300,000 deep identified without host recursion, the second nest a duplicate of the first at every level; (d) twins are convertible and near twins (one innermost argument differs, 3,000 levels down) are not, with and without class C, with and without \code{\verb~|same~}; (e) twin redexes are reduced once (class M); (f) two spellings of one binder type have one family of free variables}}
