}

\p{How the gates treat what the mode changes: nothing in M8's gate compares the mode-on machine with the mode-off machine; every comparison is inside the mode (lane against lane, lane against reference engine), where V6 makes record words and ticks comparable word for word. The mode-on / mode-off comparison is the completeness test of 10.1 (ticks) and the equal accepted / rejected / declined counts of every counter run.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{11. Recommendation and stages}

\p{\strong{Adopt a restricted form, in stages; keep the present model for everything but applications.} The evidence: no verdict needs canonical refs (sections 1, 8; five runs of M8's full gate and the hostile suite); applications are the one class whose probes are mostly wasted (9, 10.1); the gain exists where sessions are large (reachability: -17 \% warm wall clock at one worker and -10 \% at eight on the JVM; -12 \% at one worker and nothing at eight in the native image) and the price where they are small (the Cedar slice: +4 \% at one worker when every session is lazy); a rule that is lazy only where it pays leaves the library corpora exactly as they are. Measured against the owner's first number (note 12: warm wall clock with eight workers) this is a gain on one corpus class on the JVM, at the edge of the scatter, and no loss anywhere - enough for a staging switch, not yet for a default.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Stage}\th{What}\th{Owners (patch)}\th{Evidence / condition to enter}}
\tr{\td{\strong{0. Plumbing, no behaviour change}}\td{records may be outside \code{\verb~|vtab~}: \code{\verb~|vtabUsed~}, \code{\verb~|addRecordFree~}, \code{\verb~|enterRecordAt~}, growth and reset skip private bits; \code{\verb~|Values.ident~} and the force points of class K behind \code{\verb~|privMade != 0~}}\td{M6 (0002), M1 (0001)}\td{with no lazy site every counter and every word is today's (the mode-off rows of 10.1; the module's default test group with the mode off: 451 tests, 0 failures)}}
\tr{\td{\strong{1. \code{\verb~|lazyid~} as a staging switch, off in strict mode}}\td{= mode 235: \code{\verb~|MKAPP~} of code blocks lazy except the scrutinee of the next \code{\verb~|WHNF~}; classes K, M (WHNF, CORE, DELTA, VTYPE), C; adaptive sites; lazy only in sessions of 2^17 records and more}\td{M7 (0003), M3 (0004), M4 (0005), M5 (0006), M1 (0001, 0007), M6 (the switch, \code{\verb~|SWITCHES.md~}, counters into the statistics)}\td{reachability, JVM, warm: 888 against 1066 ms at one worker (-16.7 \%, ranges disjoint), 460 against 511 ms at eight (-10.0 \%; workers' CPU -10.5 \%); 2.66 M of 8.4 M record-table probes per pass not made; ticks identical to the mode-off run (9,104,125); Cedar slice, Init: counters identical to the mode-off run (the sessions never reach the threshold), Cedar slice wall clock -0.1 \% (mode 171). Gate: M8's full gate with mode 235 PASSES WITH DECLINES (\code{\verb~|machine-gate-default-u235-u235.md~}, 586 s: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0, 0 differences in the tier, convention and audit lanes, pipeline 230 / 230; ticks of reachability, Init and Std in the gate = the mode-off ticks). Native image: -11.9 \% at one worker (ranges disjoint), nothing at eight (+3.1 \%, inside the scatter). To enter the default set: M8's gate on the main tree; \strong{an eight-worker measurement with more than two processes per row on the platform that ships} (the JVM row is at the edge of its scatter and the image row shows no gain); one large corpus with giant declarations (Mathlib, not run here)}}
\tr{\td{\strong{2. Complete the classes, then widen}}\td{class M for the two flag memos (\code{\verb~|ISPROP~} / \code{\verb~|PROPT~}, \code{\verb~|PIRR~} / \code{\verb~|PROOF~}); class C for the argument pairs of \code{\verb~|CARGS~} and the lazy-delta step; the completeness test (\code{\verb~|default,-warm~}: ticks equal) becomes a gate. Only then: lower the session threshold, and every site with adaptive sites (mode 239)}\td{M4, M5, M3; M8 (the test)}\td{today +0.02 to +0.2 \% ticks (block sites), +0.07 to +0.2 \% (every site, adaptive); every-site laziness measured -16.5 \% on reachability at one worker (111), but +9 \% on the Cedar slice without adaptation (47): it must not enter without the trigger and the adaptive rule}}
\tr{\td{\strong{3. The tier}}\td{\code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~} mirrors the lazy site and the scrutinee test; "reserve, do not write" (section 5); with T3's \code{\verb~|CALL~} and direct call nodes the unit over which a private application can stay virtual is caller + callee}\td{T3 (U1 first), M1 (reservation), M8 (tier equivalence over identified records)}\td{design only. T3's U1 alone measured nothing outside the scatter (machine-T2.log 20:01Z); this stage is where its direct calls would have an object to remove}}
\tr{\td{\strong{not recommended}}\td{every site lazy without adaptation (47); lazy closures / suspensions / frames (stage D of 9.2); reclamation of private records in the stepper}\td{-}\td{10.1 (records +37 to +61 \%, ticks +1.6 to +5.9 \% on library corpora), 10.2 (+9 \%), the session-end census (2-6 \% of the suspensions are never used)}}
}

\p{What stage 1 costs if it is wrong: it is one bit test per key-forming call while a large session has private records and nothing otherwise; switching it off is \code{\verb~|rlvm.u2=0~}.}
}

\subtree{
\title{12. Not established}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Eight workers.} The gain is resolved at one worker on both platforms; at eight workers it is -8 to -10 \% on the JVM with ranges that touch, and absent in the native image, and the reason for the difference is not known (10.2).}
\li{\strong{The native image beyond one window}: reachability at one and eight workers and the Cedar slice at eight; no Cedar slice at one worker, no adaptive every-site mode beyond 239 on reachability.}
\li{\strong{Init, Std, full cedar, Mathlib, con-leche, cslib, navier-stokes-euler in a timing window.} Counters only for Init, Std and the Mathlib slice; the windows for Init / Std and full cedar with 8 workers were queued behind the quiet lock (waits of 13-27 minutes per window) and cancelled when the session ended; with the large-session trigger the counters of Init are the mode-off counters, which bounds what a timing could show.}
\li{\strong{More than two processes per row.} The scatter between two JVM processes of one configuration is up to 8 \%; the resolved rows are reachability at one worker (two windows agree) and the Cedar slice with every site lazy.}
\li{\strong{The timings are of the form before the force points were outlined} (jar \code{\verb~|f62325f62b53~} and earlier); the patches are the outlined form (\code{\verb~|7e07c389b70b~}), whose counters are identical on six runs and whose methods are smaller, but which was not timed.}
\li{\strong{The launcher path.} Every timing is \code{\verb~|WarmMain~} (one engine kept, fresh sessions per pass, no admission pipeline, no pipelined loading), not \code{\verb~|bin/rlvm -X passes=N -X passes-keep=engines~}.}
\li{\strong{The tier.} \code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~} does not know the lazy site (its \code{\verb~|MKAPP~} node interns); section 5 is design. T3's U1 and this mode were not run together.}
\li{\strong{Closures, suspensions, frames} (stage D): census only (9.2, 10.1).}
\li{\strong{Reclamation / nursery}: design only (4.4, 5 step 3); the footprint of a session grows in this mode and no run here was near a memory wall, so what the growth costs on the giant declarations of Mathlib is not known.}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|once~}} (X1) together with this mode: argued (section 6), not run - the tree of 19:04Z does not contain it.}
\li{\strong{Why the gain is what it is.} No profile was taken; "the probes that are not made" is the mechanism by construction, the share of the time it explains is not measured.}
\li{\strong{Mutants.} The four mutant corpora (17,775 exports) were not run with the mode; the hostile suite, the 230 tests and the corpora were.}
\li{\strong{A site per instruction / per term node} for the adaptive rule (the prototype's site is the head constant).}
}
}
